nesses: cooperation, attitude.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Strengths: technical competence, situational awareness, leadership. Weaknesses: feedback orientation, organization.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, also arrogant. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: attitude, leadership.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate C has strong technical and leadership but issues with criticism and organization. Candidate B has stress resilience and technical but attitude issues. Candidate A is reliable and good crew atmosphere but communication issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Long-distance pilot requires reliability, stress, technical, decision, crew cooperation, responsibility. Communication is crucial. Candidate A's communication difficulty and egocentric may be problematic. Candidate B's uncooperative and grumpy also problematic for crew. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership also problematic. Candidate C's unorganized and poor at criticism could affect safety but maybe less than communication issues? Leadership is very good. So candidate C seems best overall despite some concerns.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion (none) but can say \"Given the facts we have so far\". Provide evidence: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, very good leadership, but note concerns: not good at taking criticism, unorganized. Explain why still best.\n\nProceed."}
